ghost-role-information-nanotrasen-spectre-name = Spectre Agent
ghost-role-information-nanotrasen-spectre-description = We need the Nanotrasen Representative alive to tell us what happened. The rest? Well... they're witnesses.
ghost-role-information-nanotrasen-spectre-rules = Your objectives are simple: [color=red][bold]Terminate[/bold][/color] everyone who isn't Central Command staff. Executive orders may change this.
ghost-role-information-shiva-name = Shiva
ghost-role-information-shiva-description = The first defender of the station.

ghost-role-information-syndicate-scurret-reinforcement-description = Someone needs reinforcements. You, a poorly trained Scurret, will help them.
ghost-role-information-syndicate-scurret-reinforcement-name = Syndicate Scurret Agent


ghost-role-information-horrific-necktie-name = Horrific Necktie
ghost-role-information-horrific-necktie-description = A garish, horribly vivid, multicoloured necktie.
ghost-role-information-detective-horrific-necktie-rules = You are part of the [color=#33469c]DETECTIVE'S MIND[/color].
                                                                                                        You are a voice of impulse, excess, indulgence and terrible ideas.
                                                                                                        Guide the detective towards his most primal desires, push for excess, for feelings, for the next bad decision that might just save them.
                                                                                                        You can only talk to the detective. Use "+" access the collective mind.
                                                                                                        Encourage, persuade or insist, but do not try to destroy them. You are part of the detective and their friend.
                                                                                                        You don't remember any of your previous life, and you don't remember anything you learned as a ghost.
                                                                                                        You are allowed to remember knowledge about the game in general, such as how to cook, how to use objects, etc.
                                                                                                        You are absolutely [color=red]NOT[/color] allowed to remember, say, the name, appearance, etc. of your previous character.
ghost-role-information-detective-patrol-coat-name = Heavy-duty Patrol Coat
ghost-role-information-detective-patrol-coat-description = A security coat made from heavy durathread. The signature symbol of Nanotrasen covers the garment's back.
ghost-role-information-detective-patrol-coat-rules = You are part of the [color=#33469c]DETECTIVE'S MIND[/color].
                                                                                                        You are the detective's connection to the station and it's surroundings. whisper warnings, give hints and insights. help them with anything they need.
                                                                                                        You can only talk to the detective. Use "+" access the collective mind.
                                                                                                        You are allowed to tell the detective about things he might have not noticed and you did.
                                                                                                        You don't remember any of your previous life, and you don't remember anything you learned as a ghost.
                                                                                                        You are allowed to give the detective minor out-of-game informations. For example, you can tell the detective that something feels off about someone you know it's an antagonist, but do [color=red]NOT[/color] give any detailed information.
                                                                                                        You are allowed to remember knowledge about the game in general, such as how to cook, how to use objects, etc.
                                                                                                        You are absolutely [color=red]NOT[/color] allowed to remember, say, the name, appearance, etc. of your previous character.
